<title>UK: CSFB leads $200 million asset-backed bond.</title>
<headline>CSFB leads $200 million asset-backed bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston said on Friday it was lead manager of a $200 million deal launched in the name of Asset Backed Capital Ltd.</p>
<p>The three-year notes were reoffered to yield 15 basis points over U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  COUPON     6.875     MATURITY    02.MAY.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.2335  PAY DATE    02.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    100.046   SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMS US/GB/JP/CI</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.1875    SELL CONC  1.1875    PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.FEB.00</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
